Ram influences the team by example more than by instruction. Although he manages several projects alongside people management, he still makes time to get into the detail of what we deliver, asks the questions that make us test our assumptions, and checks that things land the way we agreed. That standard has rubbed off on the team: it is a big part of why our Bill Pay migration deliverables this year, from the associate pilot and its migration controls to the reconciliation and cleanup tooling, have landed well and drawn good feedback from partners. He also pushes people like me to try new approaches, to pick up new tools and techniques rather than wait for them, and to share what we learn with the rest of the team, which has made us more self-sufficient. The opportunity I see is simply to keep extending that reach: the more of his thinking he puts in front of partner teams and the wider program early, the more the rest of the organization benefits from the way he operates.
